How to setup SonarQube for static code analysis using GitHub Actions

🔍 About SonarQube

* SonarQube  is a code quality management tool
* It analyses the quality of the source code and then it will generate a report
* SonarQube is an open-source platform for continuous inspection of code quality. It helps developers identify bugs, code smells, vulnerabilities, and security issues in their code base
* SonarQube supports multiple programming languages and integrates with CI/CD pipelines to ensure high-quality code
* It supports multiple databases, browsers, languages and platforms
* It shows bugs, vulnerabilities, code smells etc.,
* Install AWS PostgreSQL or MySQL in production servers for persistent 
* Default Port number is 9000

🔍 Make SonarQube as system service

* Once installed SonarQube, make it as system service so that we can use systemctl commands for status, start, stop, restart, enable.
      systemctl status sonarqube
      systemctl start sonarqube
      systemctl restart sonarqube
      systemctl enable sonarqube
      systemctl stop sonarqube

🔍 Access SonarQube using DNS

* Access sonarqube using DNS name and enable https
* Launch EC2 instances in private subnet where sonarqube is installed
* For this create Target Group, Load Balancer, ACM certicate for HTTPS and use Route53 for DNS name

🔍 In SonarQube UI

* Create a project in sonarqube
* Generate sonar token
* Create Quality gate and attach to the project

🔍 In AWS

* Add sonar url and token in AWS secret manager
* Setup OIDC provider and access sonar url and sonar token

🔍 GitHub Actions workflow

* Configure selg hosted runner and install runner
* Make the runner service as system service so that systemctl commands can be used
* Use paths for filtering
  paths:
     - 'ecommerce-app/**'
     - '.github/workflows/java-sonar.yml'
* Write concurrency
concurrency:
 group: java-sonar-pr-${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}
 cancel-in-progress: true
* Use quality gate - if quality gate is failed make the merge button disabled so that the code is valid

🔍 pom.xml

* Write below properties in <properties>
    <sonar.projectKey>ecommerce-app</sonar.projectKey>
      <sonar.projectName>Ecommerce App</sonar.projectName>
* Configure below plugins
     <plugin>
            <groupId>org.sonarsource.scanner.maven</groupId>
            <artifactId>sonar-maven-plugin</artifactId>
            <version>5.7.0.6970</version>
        </plugin>

          <plugin>
            <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
            <artifactId>maven-jar-plugin</artifactId>
            <version>3.4.2</version>

Like this we can configure SonarQube for Static Analysis using GitHub actions. 
